    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕpĭmētheus</span></b> ,
			ei, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιμηθεύς</span>, in the Greek mythology, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a son of Iapetus and
				Clymene</i>, <i>the husband of Pandora</i>, Hyg.
			Fab. praef. 142.—Whence <i>his daughter
				Pyrrha</i> is called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕpĭmēthis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιμηθίς</span>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1,
				390</span></i>.</div>
